","updated_at":"2026-11-21T17:39:37Z"}],"body":"A security patch for KubeVela 1.11: **every image KubeVela ships or runs by default moves off the compromised eMudhra\nCA chains** (vela-core, vela-cli, cluster-gateway, the built-in definitions Job and the `build-push-image` kaniko\ndefault), the definitions Job image also drops the Brotli code affected by CVE-2026-111497, and a set of fixes from\nthe 1.12 release testing tightens what Applications can reach. Some of those change behaviour: read the upgrade notes\nbefore upgrading.\n\n## Security\n\n### eMudhra CA compromise and CVE-2026-111497 (Brotli)\n\n- **vela-core and vela-cli on `alpine:3.24`** (#7644). vela-cli was built on `alpine:3.15` (end of life), whose CA\n  store trusts the eMudhra / emSign roots behind the October 2026 intermediate CA compromise (14 of 14 test chains\n  verify). vela-core used a floating `alpine:3.18` tag, so whether its store was fixed depended on the day it was built.\n  Both are now `alpine:3.24` pinned by digest: none of the 14 chains verifies, and neither image contains Brotli code.\n- **cluster-gateway `v1.9.2`** (#7598). The chart ran `oamdev/cluster-gateway:v1.9.0-alpha.2` (2023), which trusts\n  all 14 compromised chains. It now runs `oamdev/cluster-gateway:v1.9.2`, pinned by digest (Alpine 3.24, all 14\n  rejected). With it the chart passes `--enable-priority-and-fairness=false` instead of the removed\n  `APIPriorityAndFairness=false` feature gate (API Priority and Fairness stays off), and in authentication mode\n  (`authentication.enabled=true`) vela-core's ClusterRole can read validating admission policies and their bindings,\n  which the newer gateway needs. vela-core and the vela CLI are built against the same tag.\n- **Built-in definitions Job on `alpine/k8s:1.34.13`** (#7645). The Job that installs the built-in definitions on\n  install and upgrade ran `alpine/k8s:1.31.13`, which ships `brotli-libs 1.1.0` (CVE-2026-111497) and trusts 7\n  of the 14 compromised chains. It now runs `alpine/k8s:1.34.13`, pinned by digest.\n- **`build-push-image` uses a maintained kaniko by default** (#7633):\n  `ghcr.io/osscontainertools/kaniko:v1.29.1@sha256:e7cba1f7e70c01c8ee1cbe622d07990c04dea550430c4c81319d26679226cd37`\n  instead of `oamdev/kaniko-executor:v1.9.1`, a copy of the archived upstream kaniko with the same CA problem. A step\n  that sets `kanikoExecutor` keeps its image.\n\n### Outbound HTTP and namespace boundaries (#7592)\n\nFrom the 1.12 release testing, backported:\n\n- **Always refused:** loopback (`127.0.0.0/8`, `::1`), unspecified (`0.0.0.0/8`, `::`) and local-use NAT64\n  (`64:ff9b:1::/48`) addresses, in addition to the cloud-metadata and link-local addresses already refused in 1.11.1.\n  `oci://` chart pulls now go through the same check.\n- **Bounded:** HTTP from the `request`, `webhook` and `notification` steps and `vela/http` in definitions times out\n  after at most `workflow.http.maxTimeout` (default `60s`; unset stays 3s) and fails on a body over\n  `workflow.http.maxResponseBytes` (default 1 MiB).\n- **The `vela-cli` step's Job runs in the Application's namespace**, as the ServiceAccount named in\n  `serviceAccountName` (default `default`), instead of in `vela-system` as vela-core.\n- **Config steps** (`read-config`, `list-config`, `create-config`, `delete-config`) stay in the Application's\n  namespace, except for shared system configs in `vela-system`.\n- **`helmchart`** reads its repository credentials and `valuesFrom` only from the Application's namespace.\n- **Terraform remote modules** are read from a bare clone, with the SSH key Secret from the definition's namespace.\n- **CUE nested more than 1000 levels** is refused before parsing, instead of being able to crash the controller.\n- The query provider never returns a Secret's data; with `authentication.withUser=false` a hand-written\n  `app.oam.dev/username` is ignored; with `authorization.definitionValidationEnabled`, referenced Workflows and\n  Policies are checked too.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- A `request` step succeeds on a reply that isn't JSON (`responseBody` holds it), and fails on an HTTP 400.\n- A definition revision an Application pins (`type@vN`) is never garbage-collected.\n- Completed `webhook` / `notification` steps no longer run again after a stale-cache conflict.\n- A `helmchart` release owned by another Application is refused instead of being overwritten on every reconcile.\n- `vela workflow rollback` continues at once instead of waiting for the next resync.\n- Lists in updated objects are replaced exactly (a removed RoleBinding subject leaves nothing behind); owned children\n  are listed in their own namespace (VelaUX's resource tree for namespace-scoped users); `vela/http` request headers\n  in templates work; webhook validation stops when the API server gives up on the request.\n- With cert-manager or a supplied certificate, the webhooks use `admissionWebhooks.failurePolicy` (`Fail`) from the\n  first install.\n\n## Upgrade notes\n\n```shell\nhelm repo update kubevela\nhelm show crds kubevela/vela-core --version 1.11.2 | kubectl apply --server-side --force-conflicts -f -   # Helm doesn't upgrade CRDs\nhelm upgrade kubevela kubevela/vela-core --version 1.11.2 -n vela-system -f <your values file>\n```\n\n- **Don't use `--reuse-values`.** From 1.11.1 it fails (`nil pointer evaluating interface {}.maxTimeout`): the new\n  `workflow.http` values are missing from the old release. Even with them set, it keeps 1.11.1's image values, so\n  cluster-gateway and the definitions Job stay on the old, unfixed images. Use your own values file, or\n  `--reset-then-reuse-values` (Helm 3.14+). If you set `multicluster.clusterGateway.image.tag` or\n  `builtinDefinitions.job.image.tag` yourself, update or remove them.\n- **`vela-cli` steps:** the Job now runs in the Application's namespace as `default` unless the step names a\n  `serviceAccountName`, and the step fails at once if that account doesn't exist. Give the account the rights the\n  command needs. An Application in `vela-system` can still name `kubevela-vela-core`.\n- **HTTP steps that may now fail:** a call to `localhost` or another loopback address (use the Service's DNS name); a\n  timeout of `0`, negative, without a unit or over 60s; a response over 1 MiB; a `request` that gets a 400. Raise the\n  bounds with `workflow.http.maxTimeout` / `workflow.http.maxResponseBytes`.\n- **Cross-namespace sources:** move `helmchart` credentials / `valuesFrom` sources, configs read by config steps,\n  and Terraform module SSH keys into the namespace that now reads them.\n- **Air-gapped installs:** mirror `oamdev/cluster-gateway:v1.9.2`, `alpine/k8s:1.34.13` and\n  `ghcr.io/osscontainertools/kaniko:v1.29.1` (by digest).\n\n## Dependencies at release tags\n\nKubeVela now requires these Go modules at release tags instead of untagged commits:\n\n- `github.com/kubevela/workflow` **`v0.7.3`** (#7658): its bounded workflow HTTP and the step TLS Secret read only from\n  the step's namespace reach vela-core; the rest of v0.7.3 is the standalone vela-workflow chart.\n- `github.com/oam-dev/cluster-gateway` **`v1.9.2`** (#7598)\n- `github.com/oam-dev/terraform-controller` **`v0.8.2`** (the Terraform `Configuration` API types; code unchanged) (#7617)\n- `github.com/oam-dev/cluster-register` **`v1.0.4`** (`vela cluster join --engine ocm`; code unchanged) (#7625)\n\n## Images\n\n- `oamdev/vela-core:v1.11.2@sha256:899a35de58c8855f55338cd530111efb438d16fee56e18e44b62696d57bf695e` (`linux/amd64`, `linux/arm64`): Alpine 3.24\n- `oamdev/vela-cli:v1.11.2@sha256:a395038fbd6fdc13a7a8f54d85ab2d65a25ac936dc26fe1545c2976195e2a00f` (`linux/amd64`, `linux/arm64`): Alpine 3.24\n- `oamdev/cluster-gateway:v1.9.2@sha256:7cc34439263689a4d11042db38ce54f5da893d8e533c01917f2450dcf11a0544`\n- `alpine/k8s:1.34.13@sha256:4011c68d73de6803987509ad1ab9520124a27e31484e3f0e45f95a74ecac7a45` (definitions Job)\n- `ghcr.io/osscontainertools/kaniko:v1.29.1@sha256:e7cba1f7e70c01c8ee1cbe622d07990c04dea550430c4c81319d26679226cd37` (`build-push-image` default)\n\n## What's Changed\n* [Backport release-1.11] Fix: move cluster-gateway to v1.9.2 for the eMudhra CA fix by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7598\n* [Backport release-1.11] Chore: require cluster-register v1.0.4 by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7625\n* [Backport release-1.11] Chore: require terraform-controller v0.8.2 by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7617\n* [Backport release-1.11] Fix: default build-push-image to a maintained kaniko image for the eMudhra CA fix by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7633\n* [Backport release-1.11] Fix: fixes from the v1.12 release testing by @briankane in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7592\n* [Backport release-1.11] Fix: move the built-in definitions Job to alpine/k8s 1.34.13 for the eMudhra CA fix by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7645\n* [Backport release-1.11] Fix: move the base images to alpine 3.24 for the eMudhra CA fix by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7644\n* [Backport release-1.11] Chore(ci): pin the remaining actions and BuildKit, and scan release branches with Trivy by @jerrinfrancis in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7650\n* [Backport release-1.11] Chore: bump kubevela/workflow to v0.7.3 by @briankane in https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/pull/7658\n\n**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/kubevela/kubevela/compare/v1.11.1...v1.11.2\n","mentions_count":2}
